---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: docs-specs-legacy-routing
purpose: "Legacy/parallel specs dir. New design specs belong in the governed home genesis/docs/superpowers/specs/ (full lifecycle gate)."
rules:
  - id: route-specs-to-governed-home
    class: dispatch
    when: { write: "*.md", new: true }
    route-to: { dest: genesis/docs/superpowers/specs/ }
    parameters:
      dispatch-agent: librarian
      dispatch-prompt: >
        Confirm whether this is genuinely a new specification and name the governed destination
        or an existing artifact to merge into. Report ROUTE, MERGE, or DROP to the editing agent;
        do not move or create files and do not derail implementation.
    why: "New specs go to genesis/docs/superpowers/specs/ where the lifecycle frontmatter gate lives — not this ungoverned legacy dir."
---
# docs/specs (legacy)

This directory predates the superpowers governance and bypasses the spec lifecycle gate. New specs are
routed (at birth) to `genesis/docs/superpowers/specs/`, where the full frontmatter gate awaits. Existing
files are left in place.
